1
00:00:00,864 --> 00:00:01,705
[SPEAKER_01]: Hi, this is Bob Payne.

2
00:00:01,745 --> 00:00:09,209
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm the chair of the Medford Energy and Environment Commissioner Committee, however you like to state that.

3
00:00:09,389 --> 00:00:17,554
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm gonna read an announcement about how we can have a remote meeting under the current Massachusetts laws.

4
00:00:18,554 --> 00:00:25,979
[SPEAKER_01]: On February 12th, 2022, Governor Baker signed into law a supplement of COVID-19 fiscal appropriations

5
00:00:26,919 --> 00:00:32,981
[SPEAKER_01]: and an extension through July 15, 2022, of certain authorizations relating to public meetings.

6
00:00:33,741 --> 00:00:42,004
[SPEAKER_01]: This new law extends the remote meeting provisions of the governor's March 12, 2020, executive order suspending certain provisions of the open meeting law.

7
00:00:42,664 --> 00:00:45,585
[SPEAKER_01]: In accordance with the 2020 executive order, this meeting

8
00:00:46,617 --> 00:00:55,702
[SPEAKER_01]: The City of Medford Energy and Environment Committee is being conducted totally via remote participation using Zoom including committee members and the public.

9
00:00:55,822 --> 00:01:09,789
[SPEAKER_01]: The use of Zoom complies with the law's requirement to provide live adequate alternative means of public access to the deliberations of the public body instead of holding meetings in a public place that is open and physically accessible to the public.

10
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:16,113
[SPEAKER_01]: Persons who would like to listen to or view this meeting while in progress may do so by using the link

11
00:01:17,021 --> 00:01:20,883
[SPEAKER_01]: that was included on the meeting agenda posted on the city of Medford website.

12
00:01:21,823 --> 00:01:33,049
[SPEAKER_01]: If despite our best efforts, we are not able to provide for real-time access, we will post a record of this meeting on the city's website in the near future at the link provided in the meeting agenda.

13
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:40,993
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, I'm gonna do a roll call of committee members and then we'll introduce guests.

14
00:01:41,213 --> 00:01:46,496
[SPEAKER_01]: Let's see, somebody is on a phone number here.

15
00:01:48,183 --> 00:01:48,663
[SPEAKER_01]: 617-504-8481.

16
00:01:48,683 --> 00:01:53,667
[SPEAKER_01]: Is that a member?

17
00:01:55,868 --> 00:01:58,250
[SPEAKER_09]: Why don't you do a roll call of the members?

18
00:01:58,270 --> 00:02:02,733
[SPEAKER_09]: Because guests don't have to introduce themselves if they don't want to.

19
00:02:02,813 --> 00:02:02,953
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

