120
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:15,730
[SPEAKER_01]: We are now to the point of administrative updates from Alicia.

121
00:08:16,351 --> 00:08:18,472
[SPEAKER_04]: Sorry, but can I ask a question to Alicia?

122
00:08:18,492 --> 00:08:25,556
[SPEAKER_04]: So Alicia, what's the official definition of an ad hoc committee?

123
00:08:25,856 --> 00:08:30,378
[SPEAKER_04]: It's the ones where the members don't get paid or there's another definition?

124
00:08:31,059 --> 00:08:44,046
[SPEAKER_09]: No, it's that the committee is created, that the mayor decides to create a committee and forms a committee without there being an ordinance or legislative act.

125
00:08:44,907 --> 00:08:56,112
[SPEAKER_09]: So many, many of the committees and boards that are formed by the, that the city has are actually created by state legislative act.

126
00:08:56,773 --> 00:09:00,354
[SPEAKER_09]: And then many of them are adopted and created by the city.

127
00:09:00,895 --> 00:09:05,557
[SPEAKER_09]: And some of which, some are both the city adopts an act of the legislature.

128
00:09:06,697 --> 00:09:12,180
[SPEAKER_09]: like the planning board, the zoning board, historic, many of those actually have some state guidelines.

129
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:16,562
[SPEAKER_09]: There are several that the city created ordinances to create.

130
00:09:18,583 --> 00:09:25,966
[SPEAKER_09]: The garden commission is the one I can think of that is a city ordinance that is not created by state act.

131
00:09:26,706 --> 00:09:34,410
[SPEAKER_09]: And then off the top of my head, I know that the bicycle commission and this committee were both created because the mayor wanted them.

132
00:09:36,519 --> 00:09:39,600
[SPEAKER_09]: And so those are ad hoc tasks or ad hoc committees.

133
00:09:40,341 --> 00:09:43,782
[SPEAKER_09]: The mayor also has the ability to create ad hoc task forces.

134
00:09:44,262 --> 00:09:49,284
[SPEAKER_09]: So a committee is typically refers to something that's longstanding.

135
00:09:49,804 --> 00:09:53,365
[SPEAKER_09]: It's created, but it's not a fixed duration.

136
00:09:53,505 --> 00:09:55,746
[SPEAKER_09]: It's to serve an ongoing purpose.

137
00:09:57,366 --> 00:10:02,008
[SPEAKER_09]: I will tell you there's been debate over the years whether or not to have an ordinance created and it,

138
00:10:03,490 --> 00:10:14,054
[SPEAKER_09]: It's gone back and forth, and a lot of the feeling was that it would create unnecessary red tape that would not necessarily give the committee any additional powers.

139
00:10:14,214 --> 00:10:16,455
[SPEAKER_09]: It would just put more rules on it.

140
00:10:18,581 --> 00:10:36,477
[SPEAKER_09]: There are, and actually that's a great segue to, I don't know if this is an administrative update or an announcement, but there are ad hoc task forces that the mayor creates, and those are typically created for a specific purpose, and usually for some limited time duration.

141
00:10:37,538 --> 00:10:39,760
[SPEAKER_09]: An example of those would be the parking

142
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:43,803
[SPEAKER_09]: task force that occurred that made recommendations around the parking committee.

143
00:10:43,903 --> 00:10:46,705
[SPEAKER_09]: So you could see one that served its full length.

