00:14:57,184 --> 00:15:01,245
[SPEAKER_09]: It's a website that we send out and you answer the questions.

193
00:15:01,965 --> 00:15:04,305
[SPEAKER_09]: Usually people are asked to do it every two years.

194
00:15:04,745 --> 00:15:09,966
[SPEAKER_09]: Gaston was asking about it because he was just appointed to the bike commission and they asked him to do that.

195
00:15:10,526 --> 00:15:12,907
[SPEAKER_09]: And he had never been asked to do it for this committee.

196
00:15:13,827 --> 00:15:18,308
[SPEAKER_09]: So if people haven't done it for this committee, we're happy to recirculate that link again.

197
00:15:20,084 --> 00:15:29,411
[SPEAKER_09]: Usually, at this point, Teresa in my office usually collects the responses and just lets the HR office know who's done it and who isn't.

198
00:15:30,392 --> 00:15:34,415
[SPEAKER_09]: As staff, we're expected to do it every two years.

199
00:15:35,596 --> 00:15:41,860
[SPEAKER_09]: So, but some years people remember to ask us and some years they don't.

200
00:15:43,301 --> 00:15:43,542
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

201
00:15:43,702 --> 00:15:45,743
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's not a critical shortcoming.

202
00:15:46,524 --> 00:15:46,684
[SPEAKER_09]: No.

203
00:15:48,710 --> 00:15:49,010
[SPEAKER_01]: Very good.

204
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:56,013
[SPEAKER_09]: But if anybody ever wonders about conflict of interest things, that's the training is interesting.

205
00:15:56,373 --> 00:15:58,314
[SPEAKER_09]: I learned stuff from it, so.

206
00:16:01,696 --> 00:16:04,837
[SPEAKER_01]: How would we, if someone wanted to do that, how would they?

207
00:16:06,378 --> 00:16:13,180
[SPEAKER_09]: I can just circulate the, I think Guesto and Teresa sent you the link.

