[SPEAKER_05]: You know, he did talk pretty fast.

964
01:31:19,489 --> 01:31:25,654
[SPEAKER_05]: I'm wondering if the other town being mentioned being to all of them, which is gas powered.

965
01:31:25,714 --> 01:31:31,978
[SPEAKER_05]: And then he also mentioned there's a house bill to help municipalities for contractors.

966
01:31:34,280 --> 01:31:34,620
[SPEAKER_05]: I don't know.

967
01:31:34,640 --> 01:31:35,901
[SPEAKER_05]: I think it needs a little more thought.

968
01:31:35,961 --> 01:31:38,423
[SPEAKER_05]: So I'm sort of on the fence.

969
01:31:38,963 --> 01:31:39,824
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, I agree.

970
01:31:39,864 --> 01:31:41,285
[SPEAKER_04]: And we have small yards.

971
01:31:41,525 --> 01:31:43,686
[SPEAKER_04]: I still maintain that we have very small yards.

972
01:31:44,827 --> 01:31:53,350
[SPEAKER_04]: see why in Medford this cannot be done with a rake if people decide to still blow their leaves or whatever it's called.

973
01:31:53,370 --> 01:31:57,751
[SPEAKER_04]: Because I agree that yes, it's not productive to do that.

974
01:31:58,471 --> 01:31:58,711
[SPEAKER_05]: Right.

975
01:31:59,092 --> 01:32:00,272
[SPEAKER_05]: And here's the other thing too.

976
01:32:00,292 --> 01:32:07,694
[SPEAKER_05]: I mean, I know a lot of people, tons of residents need landscaping services and we have them all the time in the summer.

977
01:32:08,494 --> 01:32:13,056
[SPEAKER_05]: So, you know, if we got away from leaf blowers and

978
01:32:13,721 --> 01:32:16,024
[SPEAKER_05]: the landscaping companies could still rake.

979
01:32:16,404 --> 01:32:23,532
[SPEAKER_05]: I mean, it could be sort of like what the Gaston, what you had set up for the app for our snow shovelers.

980
01:32:23,972 --> 01:32:32,762
[SPEAKER_05]: We can, maybe we could do something for, you know, lawn care volunteers or, you know, residents to help other people kind of thing.

981
01:32:37,120 --> 01:32:40,521
[SPEAKER_09]: So I would actually like to point out, I'm all in favor of your motion.

982
01:32:40,781 --> 01:32:42,042
[SPEAKER_09]: I'm all in favor of this ban.

983
01:32:43,182 --> 01:32:57,027
[SPEAKER_09]: But I feel like if the committee was gonna focus on an education committee, it ought to be on the leave the leaves and how removing the leaves at all over the winter is really impacting pollinators, butterflies.

984
01:32:58,108 --> 01:33:01,769
[SPEAKER_09]: My favorite is the winky light ones.

985
01:33:03,479 --> 01:33:04,099
[SPEAKER_05]: Fireflies?

986
01:33:04,380 --> 01:33:05,260
[SPEAKER_09]: Fireflies.

987
01:33:05,601 --> 01:33:09,023
[SPEAKER_09]: Do you know that fireflies lay their eggs in dead leaves?

988
01:33:09,764 --> 01:33:12,986
[SPEAKER_09]: And that when you rake up your leaves, you're raking away the firefly eggs.

989
01:33:13,206 --> 01:33:18,910
[SPEAKER_09]: And that's why there are no fireflies in the spring anymore because of this push to clean up the leaves all the time.

990
01:33:18,930 --> 01:33:22,613
[SPEAKER_03]: Alicia, I have an all natural backyard.

991
01:33:22,633 --> 01:33:24,114
[SPEAKER_03]: I completely agree with you.

992
01:33:24,134 --> 01:33:31,820
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't even rake until the spring and I don't do a very good job in the spring.

993
01:33:33,491 --> 01:33:44,519
[SPEAKER_03]: But I think that what we're, and so we could have an educational campaign, but I think it's a different issue.

994
01:33:45,040 --> 01:33:52,366
[SPEAKER_03]: I think what we're talking about right now is that there is an ordinance working its way through the city council

995
01:33:53,685 --> 01:33:56,168
[SPEAKER_03]: And I want that ordinance to pass.

996
01:33:57,148 --> 01:34:00,812
[SPEAKER_03]: And I hope that others here want that ordinance to pass.

997
01:34:01,512 --> 01:34:05,916
[SPEAKER_03]: I believe it will pass either four to three or five to two.

998
01:34:06,537 --> 01:34:11,181
[SPEAKER_03]: If it passes four to three, I want the mayor to not veto it.

999
01:34:11,762 --> 01:34:17,447
[SPEAKER_03]: And so that's, you know, that's completely where I'm coming from right now is that

1000
01:34:18,585 --> 01:34:19,786
[SPEAKER_03]: I wanted an ordinance.

1001
01:34:21,108 --> 01:34:25,252
[SPEAKER_03]: I'm putting a motion in favor of that ordinance and asking for the mayor's support.

1002
01:34:27,394 --> 01:34:28,936
[SPEAKER_09]: So there is a motion on the table.

1003
